Package: netkit
Type: Package
Title: Network Topology, Diffusion and Robustness Analysis
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Gallinat", email = "alex.gaoc@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for analyzing and visualizing networks, built on 'igraph'
    and returning 'ggplot2' objects rather than drawing them, so that
    diagnostics can be composed and customized. Summarizes global topology and
    per-node centrality, identifies hubs, bottlenecks and community structure,
    and classifies nodes into connectivity
    roles following Guimera and Amaral (2005) <doi:10.1038/nature03288>.
    Extracts interpretable subnetworks around a set of nodes, including
    approximate Steiner trees after Kou, Markowsky and Berman (1981)
    <doi:10.1007/BF00288961>. Propagates influence from seed nodes using
    Laplacian smoothing, heat-kernel and random-walk-with-restart diffusion,
    with degree-matched permutation nulls, and simulates network robustness
    under progressive node removal. Observed metrics, including the small-world
    coefficient, can be tested against degree-preserving random ensembles for
    statistical significance. Edge weights are supported throughout,
    with an explicit declaration of whether a weight means strength or
    distance. Matrix operations use sparse representations throughout so that
    the methods remain usable on large graphs.
